WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.620 --> 00:00:15.220
8. Hachiko Hachiko Anakita was born in 1923. When he was two months old, he went to live with

2
00:00:15.220 --> 00:00:22.120
Hide Saburo Ueno, a professor at the University of Tokyo. Hachiko and the professor lived in the

3
00:00:22.120 --> 00:00:29.360
Shibuya district of Tokyo. The professor commuted to his job on the train. Hachiko would watch the

4
00:00:29.360 --> 00:00:36.600
professor leave the house every day. And every day at 4 p.m., Hachiko would greet the professor at the

5
00:00:36.600 --> 00:00:42.920
Shibuya train station, and they would walk home together. Life was wonderful for the young dog,

6
00:00:42.920 --> 00:00:53.000
until May 21, 1925, when the professor didn't show up. Professor Ueno had suffered a stroke at work.

7
00:00:53.120 --> 00:01:00.680
He died without ever coming back to his house. Hachiko, of course, didn't know this. He waited and

8
00:01:00.680 --> 00:01:07.480
waited, and then walked home alone. He came back to the station the next day. He came back the day

9
00:01:07.480 --> 00:01:16.080
after that. He came back at 4 p.m. every day until he died nine years later. Hachiko wasn't abandoned.

10
00:01:16.080 --> 00:01:23.280
He was taken in by a new family. But Hachiko didn't want a new family. He escaped from the house and

11
00:01:23.280 --> 00:01:29.560
ran back to his old home. Eventually, Hachiko understood that the professor didn't live at the

12
00:01:29.560 --> 00:01:35.680
old house anymore. But nothing could stop the loyal dog from waiting for his master at the train

13
00:01:35.680 --> 00:01:43.640
station day in and day out. People began to recognize the big golden dog at Shibuya station.

14
00:01:43.880 --> 00:01:51.960
The station master put out food for him. One day, a former student of Professor Ueno spotted him. He

15
00:01:51.960 --> 00:01:57.880
followed Hachiko and learned his story. This student began writing articles about Hachiko.

16
00:01:57.880 --> 00:02:05.160
Soon, loyal Hachiko was famous throughout Japan. Though Hachiko himself has passed on,

17
00:02:05.160 --> 00:02:12.560
you can still see him at Shibuya station. A statue of him was erected there to honor his great heart.
